---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title={'Projects'} description={'Systems built by Phoenix I/O, including the MedTransport transportation management and dispatch platform for NEMT and ambulance providers, and a sub-millisecond trading system.'} page="projects">
<section class="page" id="p-projects" data-title="Projects">
  <div class="pagehead"><div class="wrap"><span class="label">Projects</span><h1>Built by Phoenix I/O.</h1><p class="lede">For engagements our principals led at prior firms, see <a href="/past-performance/">Past Performance</a>.</p></div></div>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="meta">
        <span class="label ember">Phoenix I/O product · Healthcare transport</span>
        <h2>MedTransport</h2>
        <p class="sub">Unified transportation management and dispatch platform</p>
        <p>An integrated operations platform for non-emergency medical transportation (NEMT) and ambulance providers, supporting ambulatory, wheelchair, stretcher, BLS and ALS services.</p>
        <p>MedTransport connects patient intake, scheduling, dispatch, crew operations, fleet management and compliance through a single, secure system. Every trip keeps a continuous, auditable record from initial booking through service completion, eliminating duplicate data entry, improving operational visibility and supporting accurate downstream billing.</p>
        <span class="label">Key platform capabilities</span>
        <ul>
          <li><b>Patient intake and scheduling.</b> Centralized patient records, coverage and authorization tracking, recurring transportation orders, automated validation and scheduling safeguards that reduce administrative errors.</li>
          <li><b>Real-time dispatch and operations.</b> An interactive dispatch board with trip assignments, vehicle locations, ETAs, shift coordination and crew-confirmed changes, giving dispatchers continuous visibility into daily operations.</li>
          <li><b>Offline-first mobile application.</b> A native Android application that lets drivers and medical crews manage assignments, record trip milestones, capture signatures, complete vehicle inspections and document incidents without continuous internet connectivity. Events synchronize securely when connectivity returns.</li>
          <li><b>Fleet and workforce compliance.</b> Centralized management of professional credentials, certification expirations, vehicle documentation, inspections, capacity restrictions and out-of-service conditions, with automated alerts and assignment-level checks.</li>
          <li><b>Security and auditability.</b> Multi-company data isolation enforced at the database level, granular role-based permissions, multi-factor authentication, encrypted patient information, hardware-backed cryptographic signatures and tamper-evident activity records.</li>
          <li><b>Integrated trip lifecycle.</b> Unified operational records designed to support electronic claims processing, payment reconciliation and electronic patient care reporting (ePCR) without duplicating information across disconnected systems.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="stackL" style="gap:20px;min-width:0">
        <div class="arch">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 440 250" role="img" aria-label="Architecture: a Kotlin Android app with signed offline sync and a server-rendered web interface connect to a centralized application service, which enforces roles and company isolation and stores data in PostgreSQL with append-only audit records.">
            <g class="n"><rect x="10" y="20" width="124" height="50" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="24" y="42">Android app</text><text x="24" y="58">Kotlin · offline</text></g>
            <g class="n"><rect x="10" y="180" width="124" height="50" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="24" y="202">Web interface</text><text x="24" y="218">server-rendered</text></g>
            <g class="n hot"><rect x="166" y="98" width="122" height="54" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="180" y="121">App service</text><text x="180" y="138">roles · isolation</text></g>
            <g class="n"><rect x="310" y="40" width="124" height="50" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="322" y="62">PostgreSQL</text><text x="322" y="78">company isolation</text></g>
            <g class="n"><rect x="310" y="160" width="124" height="50" rx="10"/><text class="t" x="322" y="182">Audit records</text><text x="322" y="198">append-only</text></g>
            <path class="flow" d="M134 45 C 152 45, 150 115, 166 115"/><path class="flow" d="M134 205 C 152 205, 150 135, 166 135"/>
            <path d="M288 115 C 300 115, 300 65, 310 65"/><path d="M288 135 C 300 135, 300 185, 310 185"/>
            <text x="178" y="90">signed sync</text>
          </svg>
          <div class="cap"><span>Kotlin · PostgreSQL · server-rendered web</span><span>Applications · Regulated data · Cryptography</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="phasetrack" aria-label="Engineering and architecture">
          <div class="pt-head"><span class="label">Engineering and architecture</span></div>
          <p>A streamlined, secure architecture: a centralized application service, a PostgreSQL database, a server-rendered web interface and a Kotlin-based Android application.</p>
          <ul>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>HIPAA-aligned security controls</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>OWASP ASVS and MASVS Level 2 mapping</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Signed offline event synchronization</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Append-only audit records</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Automated security testing</span></li>
            <li class="done"><i></i><span>Controlled deployment environments</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature">
      <div class="meta">
        <span class="label ember">Phoenix I/O project · Financial services</span>
        <h2>High-frequency trading system</h2>
        <p>A proprietary trading firm needed one platform to trade across centralized exchanges and decentralized venues, fast enough to compete and secure enough to never expose a private key.</p>
        <p class="big"><i>&lt;1</i> ms · <i>$1B+</i> volume</p>
        <ul><li>Lock-free Go distributed system with a central sequencer across 2 blockchains and 19 venues</li><li>C++ high-frequency platform with FIX, WebSocket and REST connectivity</li><li>ECDSA and Ed25519 signing with zero key exposure</li><li>Automated reconciliation and AI-assisted log analysis with human review</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arch">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 250" role="img" aria-label="Architecture: exchange, blockchain venue and market data connectors feed a lock-free sequencer that drives strategies, a signer with zero key exposure, and reconciliation.">
